# `core`'s own root file. `core` is a full ambient prelude for every other
# package (see docs/10-modules-and-linkage.md) -- its entire tree is always
# eagerly, filesystem-discovered, whether it's the package actually being
# compiled or a registered `--extern`, so nothing here needs to `import` a
# sibling submodule for it to be part of the build, be discoverable for
# `for`-extension purposes, or be reachable by any consumer. This file has
# nothing left to declare; it is the root module when `core` itself is
# compiled standalone (`just build-core`).
